== Item Weight ==
* Each item that is in an item pool has a weight associated with it. The weight represents how likely it is for the game to spawn the item. Nearly every item in the game has a weight of 1.
** For example, if there are 200 items in a given item pool, and each item has a weight of 1, that means there is a 1 in 200 (0.5%) chance to get any particular item from that pool.
** However, if an item has a weight of 0.5, that means that item is 50% as likely to spawn compared to an item that has a weight of 1. In a pool of 200 items that has only 2 items with a weight of 0.5, that would result in the total weight being 199. ((198 * 1) + (2 * 0.5) = 199) This means items with a weight of 1 have a 1 in 199 (≈0.5%) chance to spawn, while an item with a weight of 0.5 has a 1 in 398 (≈0.25%) chance to spawn.
* {{dlc|nr}} Only a few items in the game do not have a weight of 1:
** {{i|Bomber Boy}} has a weight of 0.2 in the [[Bomb Bum (Item Pool)|Bomb Bum pool]], making it 80% less likely to encounter.
** {{i|Delirious}} has a weight of 0.4 in [[Angel Room (Item Pool)|Angel Room pool]], making it 60% less likely to encounter.
** {{i|Mega Blast}} has a weight of 0.2 in the [[Devil Room (Item Pool)|Devil Room]] and [[Devil Room (Greed Mode Item Pool)|Greed Mode Devil Room]] pools, making it 80% less likely to encounter.
** {{i|Plan C}} has a weight of 0.2 in the [[Curse Room (Item Pool)|Curse Room]], [[Devil Beggar (Item Pool)|Devil Beggar]], [[Devil Room (Item Pool)|Devil Room]], [[Shop (Greed Mode Item Pool)|Greed Mode Shop]], [[Red Chest (Item Pool)|Red Chest]] and [[Shop (Item Pool)|Shop]] pools, making it 80% less likely to encounter.
* {{dlc+|r}} Item weights were adjusted more extensively in Repentance and Repentance+.
