== Weight Decrementation ==
* When you see an item spawn, the weight of that item is automatically decremented inside of the respective item pool. However, the amount of the decrementation varies depending on the specific item pool.
* If an item happens to be in more than one item pool, the weight decrementation will also apply to other pools.
* Touching an item will remove it from all item pools.
* If a pedestal cycles between multiple items, such as from {{i|Glitched Crown}}, each item option will count as being seen.

The seen items in the following item pools are decremented by 50% on sight:
* [[Beggar (Item Pool)|Beggar]]
* [[Bomb Bum (Item Pool)|Bomb Bum]]
* [[Curse Room (Item Pool)|Curse Room]] and [[Curse Room (Greed Mode Item Pool)|Greed Mode Curse Room]]
* [[Devil Beggar (Item Pool)|Devil Beggar]]
* [[Key Master (Item Pool)|Key Master]]
* {{dlc|r}} [[Battery Bum (Item Pool)|Battery Bum]]
* {{dlc|nr}} [[Shop (Item Pool)|Shop]] and [[Shop (Greed Mode Item Pool)|Greed Mode Shop]]
* {{dlc|r}} [[Mom's Chest (Item Pool)|Mom's Chest]]

The seen items in the following item pools are decremented by 40% on sight:
* [[Golden Chest (Item Pool)|Golden Chest]] and [[Golden Chest (Greed Mode Item Pool)|Greed Mode Golden Chest]]
* [[Red Chest (Item Pool)|Red Chest]]
* {{dlc|r}} [[Ultra Secret Room (Item Pool)|Ultra Secret Room]]
* {{dlc|r}} [[Old Chest (Item Pool)|Old Chest]]

The seen items in the following item pools are decremented by 10% on sight:
* [[Library (Item Pool)|Library]] and [[Library (Greed Mode Item Pool)|Greed Mode Library]]
* {{dlc|r}} [[Crane Game (Item Pool)|Crane Game]]

All other item pools not listed above are fully decremented on sight, and thus, removed.

=== Examples ===
* All items in the Treasure Room pool are completely decremented on sight. Thus, seeing a {{i|Notched Axe}} in the Basement 1 Treasure Room will make it impossible to spawn another Notched Axe in the run. (In this case, players do '''not''' have to touch the Notched Axe in order to prevent the game from ever spawning another one.)
* {{dlc|nr}} All items in the shop pool are decremented by 0.5 on sight. Thus, if you use a [[Restock Machine]] to reroll a {{i|Treasure Map}}, you have a chance for another Treasure Map to appear. However, after the Treasure Map has already appeared twice on a run, it is completely decremented from the shop pool and it will never appear again.
** {{dlc|r}} All items in the shop pool are fully decremented on sight. Thus, if you use a [[Restock Machine]] to reroll a {{i|Treasure Map}}, it will never appear again for the rest of the run.
* If the player sees {{i|Telepathy For Dummies}} in the Basement 1 Treasure Room, it is completely removed from all other pools for the rest of the run even without touching it. Seeing it in a Library and not touching it, however, allows it still to be encountered as a Treasure item, with slightly lowered weight.

== {{dlc+|nr}} Unused Item Pools ==
In the <code>itempools.xml</code> file, we can see that there are some unused item pools:
* <code>bossrush</code> - Likely intended to be used for the [[Boss Rush]]. However, in the actual game, the Boss Rush draws from the [[Treasure Room (Item Pool)|Treasure Room pool]].
* <code>challenge</code> - Likely intended to be used for [[Challenge Room]]s. However, in the actual game, Challenge Rooms draw from the [[Treasure Room (Item Pool)|Treasure Room pool]].
* <code>dungeon</code> - Likely intended to be used for the [[Crawl Space]]s. However, in the actual game, Crawl Spaces draw from the [[Treasure Room (Item Pool)|Treasure Room pool]].
