== Set Drops ==
* Some specific collectible items are hard-coded to have a chance to drop from certain special events. These are referred to as "set drops".
* {{dlc|nr}} Set drops from the [[Seven Deadly Sins]] are not affected by item pools. For example, if you touch {{i|The Virus}} in the Treasure Room on Basement 1, and then you fight [[Lust]] in the Mini-Boss Room of Basement 2, Lust will still have the normal chance to drop {{i|The Virus}}. If it does, you can take it and have two Viruses.
* Set drops from most [[Machines]] can be obtained multiple times.
** With the exception of {{i|IV Bag}}, {{i|Redemption}}, and {{i|Skatole}}.
*** If an {{i|IV Bag}} has already been touched ({{dlc|r}} or seen), then {{m|Blood Donation Machine}}s will only spawn {{i|Blood Bag}}s after.
* Set drops from bosses will always replace the [[Boss (Item Pool)|Boss Room Item]] if the set drop wasn't already obtained or depleted from pools, with some exceptions.
** {{e|Famine}}, {{e|Pestilence}}, {{e|War}}, and {{e|Death}} will always drop {{i|Cube of Meat}} or {{i|Ball of Bandages}}, even if either was already obtained.
*** {{dlc|nr}} Respectively, if {{i|A Pony}} or {{i|White Pony}} have been touched, then {{e|Headless Horseman}} and {{e|Conquest}} will drop a [[Boss (Item Pool)|Boss Room Item]] instead.
*** {{dlc|r}} Respectively, if {{i|A Pony}} or {{i|White Pony}} have been touched, then {{e|Headless Horseman}} and {{e|Conquest}} will always drop either {{i|Cube of Meat}} or {{i|Ball of Bandages}}.
** {{dlc|nr}} {{e|Krampus}} will always spawn either {{i|Head of Krampus}} or {{i|A Lump of Coal}}, even if either was already obtained.
** {{dlc|r}} {{e|Krampus}} will only spawn {{i|Head of Krampus}} once, then will only spawn {{i|A Lump of Coal}} after, even if it was already obtained.
** {{e|Mom}} will always drop {{i|The Polaroid}} and {{i|The Negative}} if they are unlocked, even if either was already obtained.
** {{dlc+|r}} {{e|Bumbino}} will drop his items in addition to the boss room item, and will always drop {{i|The Poop}} once all his drops are obtained.{{dlc-}}
** {{dlc+|r}} {{e|Hornfel}} will drop his items in addition to the boss room item, and will only drop 3 bombs once all his drops are seen.{{dlc-}}
* {{i|Sacrificial Altar}}'s drops are deceptively not from the [[Devil Room (Item Pool)|Devil Room Pool]], and are considered set drops.
** Once all of its drops are seen, it will always drop {{i|Pentagram}}.
* All other set drops not mentioned above can only spawn if the item hasn't already been obtained or depleted from pools.

